<title>UK: IBCA rates Korea Dev Bank's global bond AA minus.</title>
<headline>IBCA rates Korea Dev Bank's global bond AA minus.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European credit rating agency, said on Thursday it assigned a long-term rating of AA minus to Korea Development Bank's $500 million global bond issue.</p>
<p>&quot;The Korea Development Bank (KDB) is Korea's premier bank, playing an important role in mobilising funds to promote the development of Korean industry,&quot; IBCA said in a statement.</p>
<p>The KDB is wholly-owned by the government of Korea and , while its liabilities are not specifically guaranteed by the state, the KDB law in effect requires that the government maintain the bank's solvency, IBCA said.</p>
<p>--International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 4041</p>
